WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
Your brain runs on glucose.

2
00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:05.960
It depends on a steady supply
more than any other organ.

3
00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:09.940
But after a meal, glucose pours
into the blood from your gut.

4
00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.670
Scattered through the pancreas
sit tiny islands of cells.

5
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:18.750
So you eat a sugary snack, yet your
blood sugar barely changes for long.

6
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.320
What pulls it back?

7
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.780
In this mission, you'll find
out what raises blood glucose,

8
00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.270
and what lowers it.

9
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.180
Then you'll zoom into those islands, and
meet the two kinds of cell inside them.

10
00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:35.000
Your mission: find out what pulls your
blood sugar back after a sugary snack.
